        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Directory sharing needs a way to detect failed watcher startup, so this adds an optional error return to` vim._watch.watch()`.\r\nAutoread uses it to preserve existing file watchers when starting the shared directory watcher fails, and to avoid recording failed watchers as active.\r\nThis doesn’t add retries or user-facing failure notifications. Maybe it should be done in separate pr first? (error returns/recovery and so on)\r\n\r\nNeovim’s internal LSP watcher code could also consume the returned startup error for some recovery logic (though each M._watchfunc should follow one contract):\r\n```lua\r\nif vim.fn.has('win32') == 1 or vim.fn.has('mac') == 1 then\r\n  M._watchfunc = watch.watch\r\nelseif vim.fn.executable('inotifywait') == 1 then\r\n  M._watchfunc = watch.inotify\r\nelse\r\n  M._watchfunc = watch.watchdirs\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal cancel = M._watchfunc(...) -- omitting error right now\r\ntable.insert(cancels[client_id][reg.id], cancel)\r\n```",
